description.narrative:
Riyadh is the capital city of Saudi Arabia. Although the city has seen rapid growth and development over the last thirty years, many areas of the city are experiencing urban sprawl, increased urbanization, and high levels of crime. While it is known as the heart of the city and has high potential to become an economic centre of the city and a diverse and vibrant area, Central Riyadh has many neighbourhoods which display substandard conditions and need revitalization. The government of Saudi Arabia is willing to address these urban development challenges with initiatives such as the Future Saudi Cities Programme implemented by UN-Habitat to integrate sustainable urbanization practices in relation to city redevelopment planning or the Central Riyadh Redevelopment and Regeneration Programme for the regeneration of Central Riyadh.  

The Central Riyadh Redevelopment and Regeneration Programme is a major intervention by the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia - implemented through the Saudi Arabia Public Investment Fund by the Central Arriyadh Development Company (CADC). The programme aims at enhancing the urban environment in the region with a goal to improving the quality of life for all in the capital city of Riyadh. The Programme targets 19 neighbourhoods in the central area of Riyadh and aims by 2040 to create a “A vibrant City Center, a hub for knowledge, rich in heritage and culture, seeking to meet everyone’s expectations” through:

•	Establishing the capacities for city management and the formation of new regulations; 
•	Re-align the area with updated infrastructure and public spaces; 
•	The creation of new districts and the establishment and renovation of public utilities; 
•	Invest in new quality income generating assets; 
•	Implementation of social economic development programs.  

The current programme is preparing its second phase of work, including (a) updating the current framework plan for the site that was developed in 2012, (b) developing social and economic projects to ensure communities benefit from the developments at neighbourhood level, and (c).

The CADC requested UN-Habitat to provide technical assistance to ensure the sustainability of intervention and its alignment with international best practices for urban regeneration. UN-Habitat team conducted a scoping mission to Riyadh in January 2019 to understand in depth the context and provide technical support to the implementation of The Central Riyadh Redevelopment and Regeneration Programme. UN-Habitat team gathered expertise in the areas of urban regeneration projects, urban economy, housing and regional experience in the Arab region including projects implemented in Saudi Arabia. 

The mission enabled UN-Habitat to share success stories at global level on five key areas (i) policy and regulatory framework for an enabling environment; (ii) cultural heritage and tourism;  (iii) community engagement and job creation;  (iv) affordable housing and relocation guidelines; (v) infrastructure, investment and land value capture; and to provide initial technical feedback on the programme implementation and outlined recommendations and suggested actions in 4 key areas aligned with the implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) – leaving no one behind, reduction of spatial inequalities and urban poverty and the principles outlined in the New Urban Agenda:

•	Community and stakeholder engagement; 
•	Finance and business models and quick win projects; 
•	Enabling environment and citywide approach; 
•	Replication and learning through knowledge management. 
Following the recommendations of UN-Habitat’s mission, CADC requested an initial technical support from UN-Habitat aligned with the areas of work – Community and Stakeholder Engagement & Urban Regeneration Inclusive Impact & Mitigation Strategy Development.
